 essays:[['Explain how a trace table helps a programmer understand an algorithm.','A trace table records variable and output values after each instruction, making it easier to follow sequence, decisions and repetitions and locate errors.',['records','variables','outputs','instructions','errors']],['Compare integer, float, string and Boolean data types.','Integer stores whole numbers, float stores numbers with fractional parts, string stores text, and Boolean stores true or false. The chosen type should match the data.',['integer','whole numbers','float','string','Boolean']],['Describe how string slicing and concatenation are used.','Slicing extracts a selected part of a string using positions or indexes. Concatenation joins strings; conversions may be needed when joining text and numbers.',['slicing','part','index','concatenation','convert']],['Explain how to create a simple shape using turtle graphics.','Move the turtle forward by a set distance, turn by the required angle and repeat the commands for the required number of sides. For a regular shape, the exterior turn is 360 divided by the number of sides.',['forward','turn','angle','repeat','sides']]]
